Subject: [PATCH 4/4] peak_finder::Simple: skip rows that cannot raise the peak

The scalar loop tracks the peak index and does not vectorize. Compute each
row's maximum first with independent lanes, which vectorizes, and run the
original scan only on rows whose maximum exceeds the current peak. Same
first-index tie-breaking and NaN handling; 8x faster on a 2048^2 image
without the AVX path. Bitwise identical results.

diff --git a/cpp/math/peak_finder.cc b/cpp/math/peak_finder.cc
index f4fc142..8f409df 100644
--- a/cpp/math/peak_finder.cc
+++ b/cpp/math/peak_finder.cc
